# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated state. None of this is source.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Every package and project writes its runtime state into a `state/` dir next
# to its code. These files churn constantly (status.json is rewritten every 5
# seconds), they are machine-specific, and several of them contain a verbatim
# record of what you were working on -- session names, per-session costs,
# working directories, and LLM-judged verdicts on your own thinking blocks.
# They are regenerated from scratch on first run. Never commit them.
state/
*.lock
*.log

# Belt-and-braces: the specific files, by their real paths. Deliberately not
# bare globs like `**/index.json` -- a pattern that broad would silently
# swallow a legitimate source file with the same name later on.
packages/token-monitor-core/state/
projects/usage-history-rollups/state/
projects/cost-anomaly-alerts/state/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local overrides
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# config.local.js lets you point LLAMA_SERVER_EXE / model paths at wherever
# your build actually lives without dirtying the tracked config.
**/config.local.js
.env
.env.local

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor / OS noise
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# There is deliberately no package.json anywhere in this suite (see README),
# but if a future component ever grows one, its deps do not belong here.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Draft primers for work not started. Local scratch, deliberately untracked:
# they are speculative, they name mechanisms that have not been tested, and
# half of them will be wrong. Promote one into projects/ when it is real.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
next-ideas/
